course: dictionary
lesson: 7706
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so the word alone cannot tell you which one to use. Look at the words around it, which is its context. «Some asteroids are dark and rich in carbon, some are stony, and a few are mostly metal, like the asteroid Psyche.» The sentence is about space rocks, so Psyche here is the name of one particular asteroid.
explain: Then try the meaning in the sentence to check it fits. Your psyche is your mind and soul: your thoughts, feelings and the deep part of who you are. A frightening event can «leave a mark on her psyche», which means it changes how she thinks and feels inside.
explain: A capital P is another clue. Psyche can be a name, and in Greek myths Psyche was a beautiful young woman who fell in love with Cupid and became a goddess of the soul. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask which meaning fits the sentence best.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: Your psyche is your mind and soul: your thoughts, feelings and the deep part of who you are.
fact: Psychology, the study of the mind, comes from the same Greek word as psyche.
fact: In Greek myths, Psyche was a beautiful young woman who fell in love with Cupid (Eros).
fact: Psyche is also the name of a metal-rich asteroid, and NASA sent a mission to visit it.
exercise: «Some asteroids are dark and rich in carbon, some are stony, and a few are mostly metal, like the asteroid Psyche.» What is Psyche in this sentence? | A kind of cloud | *A metal-rich asteroid in space | A word for a nervous feeling | A sad poem about the sea
exercise: «A frightening event can leave a mark on her psyche.» What does psyche mean here? | *Her mind, thoughts and feelings | Her hair or skin | Her favourite game | Her shoes
exercise: In Greek myths, who did Psyche fall in love with? | A king of the sea | *Cupid | Zeus | Apollo
test: What does your psyche mean? | *Your mind and soul, your thoughts and feelings | A type of rock | Your favourite food | Your heartbeat
test: Which sentence uses psyche as a name? | Psychology is the study of the mind | The storm left a mark on her psyche | *Psyche was a young woman in a Greek myth who fell in love with Cupid | Her psyche felt calm and happy
exam: In «a frightening event can leave a mark on her psyche», what does psyche mean? | *Her mind and inner self | Her favourite colour | Her spare pair of socks | A type of dog
